---
interface Props {
  service?: any;
}
const { service } = Astro.props;
import '../../styles/environmental-graphics.css';
---

  <section class="sig-hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
    <div class="sig-hero__media">
      <img src="/anacostia-exhibit-wall-mu13p5yi-dm4c.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" style="width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;display:block" />
    </div>
    <div class="sig-hero__scrim" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="epi-container sig-hero__inner">
      <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <ol class="sig-crumbs">
          <li><a href="/">Home</a></li>
          <li aria-hidden="true">/</li>
          <li><a href="/services">Services</a></li>
          <li aria-hidden="true">/</li>
          <li aria-current="page">Environmental Graphics</li>
        </ol>
      </nav>
      <p class="sig-kicker">From Concept to Execution we make a Space tell its own Story.</p>
      <h1 class="epi-display-2 sig-hero__title" id="hero-title">Environmental graphics that turn walls, glass and floors into an immersive experience.</h1>
      <p class="sig-hero__lede">EPI-Colorspace designs, prints and installs murals, glass films, floor graphics and interior wayfinding for museums, universities, commercial real estate and corporate environments across the DMV. We work with the architecture rather than over it, and we install without closing the building.</p>
      <div class="sig-hero__actions">
        <a class="epi-btn epi-btn--lg" href="#start">Start Your Project</a>
        <a class="epi-btn epi-btn--lg epi-btn--outline-inverse" href="/projects">See our Projects</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="sig-hero__rule" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  </section>

  <section class="sig-section" aria-labelledby="intro-title">
    <div class="epi-container sig-split">
      <div class="sig-split__copy">
        <h2 class="epi-h1" id="intro-title">For over 20 years, EPI-Colorspace has been a trusted partner for graphics that have to live inside a working building.</h2>
        <p>We specialize in transforming a wide variety of spaces, from museums and universities to commercial real estate and corporate environments, into dynamic, immersive brand experiences. Environmental graphics are the layer that makes a room legible: where you are, whose space this is and what happens here.</p>
        <p>The craft is in the survey. Wall texture, glass mullions, floor sealer and light all decide the material before the artwork does, which is why our installs hold up years after the reveal.</p>
        <dl class="sig-facts">
          <div>
            <dt>Surfaces</dt>
            <dd>Wall, glass, floor</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Install</dt>
            <dd>Occupied buildings</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Scope</dt>
            <dd>Survey to punch walk</dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
      </div>
      <figure class="sig-frame">
        <img src="/blue-lobby-displays-mu13q4jd-onxx.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" style="width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;display:block" />
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sig-section sig-section--warm" id="zones" aria-labelledby="zones-title">
    <div class="epi-container">
      <div class="sig-head">
        <h2 class="epi-h1" id="zones-title">Four surfaces that change how a space reads.</h2>
        <p>Most programs use two or three of these together, scoped floor by floor so the budget follows the traffic.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="env-zones">
        <article class="env-zone">
          <figure class="env-zone__media">
            <img src="/spiral-lobby-graphics-mu13h9gi-cfz7.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" style="width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;display:block" />
          </figure>
          <h3>Wall murals and supergraphics</h3>
          <p>Full-height photography, typography and pattern printed at final size and seam-mapped around outlets, doors and switches.</p>
          <p class="env-zone__spec">Textured wall vinyl, matte</p>
        </article>
        <article class="env-zone">
          <figure class="env-zone__media">
            <img src="/colonial-one-windows-mu13royg-84om.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" style="width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;display:block" />
          </figure>
          <h3>Glass and privacy films</h3>
          <p>Frosted bands, gradient patterns and branded manifestation that meet visibility requirements without closing a room off.</p>
          <p class="env-zone__spec">Etch film, first surface print</p>
        </article>
        <article class="env-zone">
          <figure class="env-zone__media">
            <img src="/retail-window-wrap-mu13ikr7-460d.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" style="width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;display:block" />
          </figure>
          <h3>Floor graphics and paths</h3>
          <p>Slip-rated prints for wayfinding routes, exhibit paths and activations, applied to concrete, terrazzo, tile and carpet.</p>
          <p class="env-zone__spec">R10 slip rating</p>
        </article>
        <article class="env-zone">
          <figure class="env-zone__media">
            <img src="/building-facade-graphics-mu13937x-72if.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" style="width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;display:block" />
          </figure>
          <h3>Interior wayfinding and room ID</h3>
          <p>Level numbering, room identification and ADA tactile signage produced in house and installed as one coordinated system.</p>
          <p class="env-zone__spec">Grade 2 braille</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sig-section sig-section--ink" id="how" aria-labelledby="how-title">
    <div class="epi-container env-apply">
      <div class="sig-head">
        <h2 class="epi-h1" id="how-title">How a graphics program goes in without closing the floor.</h2>
        <p>Six practical steps between an approved concept and a finished wall. Nothing here is a surprise on install day.</p>
        <p><a class="epi-btn" href="#start">Start Your Project</a></p>
      </div>
      <ol class="env-steps">
        <li>
          <h3>Survey the surface</h3>
          <p>Texture, paint age, glass type and floor sealer are recorded, because they decide the media before the artwork does.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Map the seams</h3>
          <p>Panels are planned around outlets, corners and door frames so no seam lands in the middle of a face or a word.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Proof on the real media</h3>
          <p>Color is approved on the substrate that ships, not on a screen or a coated sheet.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Print and finish</h3>
          <p>Output up to <span class="epi-mono">126 in</span> wide, laminated and trimmed, then labeled by wall and sequence.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Install off hours</h3>
          <p>Badged crews, floor protection down, and the area cleaned so the space is usable the next morning.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Walk and document</h3>
          <p>Punch list, as-built photos and care notes, plus artwork kept on file for reprints and tenant changes.</p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sig-section" id="impact" aria-labelledby="impact-title">
    <div class="epi-container env-impact">
      <div class="sig-split__copy">
        <h2 class="epi-h1" id="impact-title">Graphics that work for the people using the building every day.</h2>
        <p>An environmental program is judged on a Tuesday afternoon, not at the reveal. These are the tests we design against.</p>
        <ul class="env-impact__list">
          <li><span><strong>Legibility first:</strong> Type sized for the real viewing distance, with contrast that holds under the lighting already installed.</span></li>
          <li><span><strong>Durable where it is touched:</strong> Heavier laminates at corridor corners, elevator lobbies and any surface within arm's reach.</span></li>
          <li><span><strong>Reversible where it matters:</strong> Removable films in leased space, documented so the wall comes back clean at the end of the term.</span></li>
          <li><span><strong>Made to change:</strong> Artwork, dimensions and materials kept on file, so a reprint is a service call rather than a new project.</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <figure class="sig-frame sig-frame--wide">
        <img src="/colonial-one-windows-mu13royg-84om.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" style="width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;display:block" />
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sig-section sig-section--warm" id="work" aria-labelledby="work-title">
    <div class="epi-container">
      <div class="sig-head">
        <h2 class="epi-h1" id="work-title">Spaces we have transformed.</h2>
        <p>Filter by surface to see the kind of program that fits your building.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="sig-filters" role="group" aria-label="Filter projects by surface">
        <button class="sig-filter" type="button" data-filter="all" aria-pressed="true">All work</button>
        <button class="sig-filter" type="button" data-filter="mural" aria-pressed="false">Murals</button>
        <button class="sig-filter" type="button" data-filter="glass" aria-pressed="false">Glass</button>
        <button class="sig-filter" type="button" data-filter="floor" aria-pressed="false">Floor</button>
        <button class="sig-filter" type="button" data-filter="wayfinding" aria-pressed="false">Wayfinding</button>
      </div>
      <div class="sig-gallery" id="gallery">
        <article class="sig-shot" data-category="mural">
          <figure class="sig-shot__frame"><img src="/commanders-building-banner-mu13c8xa-kpu3.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" style="width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;display:block" /></figure>
          <h3>Atrium supergraphic, Washington DC</h3>
          <p>3 stories, 9 panels</p>
        </article>
        <article class="sig-shot" data-category="glass">
          <figure class="sig-shot__frame"><img src="/colonial-one-windows-mu13royg-84om.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" style="width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;display:block" /></figure>
          <h3>Conference glass film program, Arlington</h3>
          <p>62 panels, gradient etch</p>
        </article>
        <article class="sig-shot" data-category="floor">
          <figure class="sig-shot__frame"><img src="/parking-notice-sign-mu13jclv-qgtf.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" style="width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;display:block" /></figure>
          <h3>Visitor path floor graphics, Baltimore</h3>
          <p>120 decals, R10 rated</p>
        </article>
        <article class="sig-shot" data-category="wayfinding">
          <figure class="sig-shot__frame"><img src="/building-facade-graphics-mu13937x-72if.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" style="width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;display:block" /></figure>
          <h3>Interior wayfinding system, Northern Virginia</h3>
          <p>84 sign types, ADA compliant</p>
        </article>
        <article class="sig-shot" data-category="mural">
          <figure class="sig-shot__frame"><img src="/spiral-lobby-graphics-mu13h9gi-cfz7.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" style="width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;display:block" /></figure>
          <h3>Cafeteria feature wall, Silver Spring</h3>
          <p>Textured vinyl, 32 ft run</p>
        </article>
        <article class="sig-shot" data-category="glass">
          <figure class="sig-shot__frame"><img src="/real-estate-banner-mu12q7mf-0tjm.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" style="width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;display:block" /></figure>
          <h3>Storefront window system, Silver Spring</h3>
          <p>Frosted and first-surface vinyl</p>
        </article>
      </div>
      <p class="sig-empty" id="gallery-empty" hidden>No projects for that surface yet. Ask us for recent examples.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sig-section" aria-label="Company at a glance">
    <div class="epi-container">
      <div class="sig-stats">
        <div>
          <p class="sig-stat__value">20+</p>
          <p class="sig-stat__label">Years designing, printing and installing graphics in the DMV</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="sig-stat__value">126</p>
          <p class="sig-stat__label">Inches of print width, so most murals run with fewer seams</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="sig-stat__value">1</p>
          <p class="sig-stat__label">Shop handling design, print, finishing and installation</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="sig-stat__value">0</p>
          <p class="sig-stat__label">Business days of downtime when we phase an install off hours</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sig-section sig-section--warm" id="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
    <div class="epi-container sig-spec">
      <div class="sig-head">
        <h2 class="epi-h1" id="faq-title">Answers before you take it to facilities.</h2>
        <p>The questions building and marketing teams ask us most, answered plainly.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="sig-acc" id="accordion">
        <div class="sig-acc__item">
          <h3>
            <button class="sig-acc__trigger" type="button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="acc-1">
              Will a mural stick to our wall texture?
              <span class="sig-acc__mark" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </button>
          </h3>
          <div class="sig-acc__panel" id="acc-1">
            <p>Lightly textured drywall takes conformable film well. Heavy orange peel, knockdown and block need either a specialty conformable media or a skim coat first. We test a sample on your wall before committing the whole program.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="sig-acc__item">
          <h3>
            <button class="sig-acc__trigger" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="acc-2">
              How long do floor graphics last?
              <span class="sig-acc__mark" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </button>
          </h3>
          <div class="sig-acc__panel" id="acc-2" hidden>
            <p>Six to twelve months in a busy corridor with a slip-rated overlaminate, longer in lower traffic. Sealed concrete and terrazzo hold up best. Carpet requires a different adhesive system, which we specify from the survey.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="sig-acc__item">
          <h3>
            <button class="sig-acc__trigger" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="acc-3">
              Do glass films meet code for visibility?
              <span class="sig-acc__mark" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </button>
          </h3>
          <div class="sig-acc__panel" id="acc-3" hidden>
            <p>Yes, when they are designed to. Manifestation bands are set at the heights your jurisdiction requires and documented on the elevation drawings, so the design intent and the code requirement are settled in the same review.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="sig-acc__item">
          <h3>
            <button class="sig-acc__trigger" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="acc-4">
              Can you install while the building is occupied?
              <span class="sig-acc__mark" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </button>
          </h3>
          <div class="sig-acc__panel" id="acc-4" hidden>
            <p>That is how most of this work goes in. Crews are badged and cleared with building management, work evenings, weekends or one floor at a time, and leave the space clean and usable before staff return.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="sig-acc__item">
          <h3>
            <button class="sig-acc__trigger" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="acc-5">
              What files do you need to start?
              <span class="sig-acc__mark" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </button>
          </h3>
          <div class="sig-acc__panel" id="acc-5" hidden>
            <p>Vector artwork in <span class="epi-mono">.ai</span>, <span class="epi-mono">.eps</span> or <span class="epi-mono">.pdf</span>, brand standards and a floor plan if you have one. Raster art should be supplied at final size with <span class="epi-mono">0.125 in</span> bleed. Large sets can be dropped through our file transfer link rather than email.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sig-section" aria-label="Client feedback">
    <div class="epi-container">
      <figure class="sig-quote">
        <div class="sig-quote__mark" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <blockquote>They surveyed the walls, told us which two would not take a mural, and proposed glass film instead. The result looks intentional because someone actually looked at the building first.</blockquote>
        <figcaption>Facilities director, university campus, Maryland</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sig-section sig-cta" id="start" aria-labelledby="start-title">
    <div class="epi-container sig-cta__inner">
      <div class="sig-split__copy">
        <h2 class="epi-h1" id="start-title">Tell us which surfaces you are looking at.</h2>
        <p>Send a floor plan, a scope or a photo of the wall. We bring visions to life, and we will tell you honestly what the surface and your schedule allow.</p>
        <p><a href="tel:3019902666" style="color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:3px">301.990.2666</a></p>
      </div>
      <form class="sig-form" id="project-form" novalidate>
        <p class="sig-form__status" id="form-status" role="status" hidden></p>
        <div>
          <label for="f-name">Name</label>
          <input id="f-name" name="name" type="text" autocomplete="name" required>
        </div>
        <div>
          <label for="f-email">Work email</label>
          <input id="f-email" name="email" type="email" autocomplete="email" required>
        </div>
        <div>
          <label for="f-surface">Surface</label>
          <select id="f-surface" name="surface">
            <option>Wall murals and supergraphics</option>
            <option>Glass and privacy films</option>
            <option>Floor graphics</option>
            <option>Interior wayfinding</option>
            <option>Not sure yet</option>
          </select>
        </div>
        <div>
          <label for="f-site">Building city</label>
          <input id="f-site" name="site" type="text" autocomplete="address-level2">
        </div>
        <div class="sig-form__full">
          <label for="f-scope">Scope and target date</label>
          <textarea id="f-scope" name="scope" required></textarea>
        </div>
        <div class="sig-form__full">
          <button class="epi-btn epi-btn--block" type="submit">Start Your Project</button>
          <p class="sig-form__note" style="margin-top:var(--space-3)">Have artwork already? Mention it and we will send a file transfer link.</p>
        </div>
      </form>
    </div>
  </section>
